<pdd-reason>Bunches are library-level knowledge reusable across plans, so they need a collection surface independent of any one plan.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "api",
  "api": {
    "endpoints": [
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/bunches",
        "auth": "none",
        "requestSchema": "?track_id=",
        "responseSchema": "{bunches: [{bunch_id, label, ordered, notes, members: [{track_id, title, artist, position}]}]}"
      },
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/bunches",
        "auth": "none",
        "requestSchema": "{label, track_ids: string[], ordered: bool, notes?}",
        "responseSchema": "{bunch_id, label, members}",
        "errors": [
          "400 fewer than 2 members"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>brain/bunch_store_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/api_router_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_bunches_collection.py` as the GET lists library bunches hydrated with member titles; ?track_id= filters to bunches containing a track. POST {label, track_ids[], ordered, notes} creates one. FEWER THAN 2 MEMBERS IS A 400. CREATING A BUNCH THAT OVERLAPS AN EXISTING ONE SUCCEEDS, deliberately: disjointness is a property of one ordering, not of the library, and a store that refused overlap would make it impossible to record both 'A then B is great' and 'B then C is great'. LIBRARY-SCOPED: journals nothing, because a new bunch constrains no plan until module 28 activates it. Per-call sqlite3 connection with timeout.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

GET lists library bunches hydrated with member titles; ?track_id= filters to bunches containing a track. POST {label, track_ids[], ordered, notes} creates one. FEWER THAN 2 MEMBERS IS A 400. CREATING A BUNCH THAT OVERLAPS AN EXISTING ONE SUCCEEDS, deliberately: disjointness is a property of one ordering, not of the library, and a store that refused overlap would make it impossible to record both 'A then B is great' and 'B then C is great'. LIBRARY-SCOPED: journals nothing, because a new bunch constrains no plan until module 28 activates it. Per-call sqlite3 connection with timeout.

